PredecessorNumber [SimTalk]
Sets the number of the predecessor object which delivers the material to the Portioner designated by
<Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.PredecessorNumber:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Example
MyPortioner.PredecessorNumber := 2
See also
Fluid from Predecessor [text box]
DePortioner
DePortioner
Use the object DePortioner to empty incoming parts of bulk goods or fluids, create a fluid out of it, and
feed the resulting fluids into a Pipe.
Image
Description
We provide three ways of defining the fluid that is to be created:
• By a fixed material and a fixed amount for every MU. For this setting you can enter the Material and the
Amount per MU.
PredecessorNumber [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-2909
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• By the MU Name depending on the MU names that are defined in the Mapping Table.
• By the MU Attribute, for which you can enter the Material Attribute and the Amount Attribute of the
MU.
When the created fluid flows out of the DePortioner into a Pipe, the MU that delivered it will be deleted.
If the outflow of fluids is interrupted, caused by a failure, a pause, or because the successor cannot accept
anything at the moment, the Exporters will not be released.
You can, for example, use the DePortioner to empty barrels of fluids or bulk goods, which are then used as
ingredients for mixed goods down your production line, and feed the material into Pipes.
You can think of the DePortioner as the counterpart of the Portioner.
To show a tooltip with information about the DePortioner, hover with the mouse over it.
To change the length of the graphic and the anchor points of the Portioner, click Show Manipulators 
on the Edit ribbon tab or press M on the keyboard.
Add the Object to the Simulation Model
To add the object DePortioner to your simulation model, click 
  Manage Class Library > Basic Objects >
Fluids > DePortioner on the Home ribbon tab.
Compare the sample models: Click the Window ribbon tab, click Start Page > Getting Started > Example
Models > Small Examples. Then, select the respective Category, the Topic, and the Example in the
dialog Examples Collection, and click Open Model.
DePortioner
